# Purpose: Prevent generated dependencies, secrets, local runtime data, and agent worktrees from entering git.
# Caller: Git status/add/commit workflows for this CCTV repository.
# Deps: Project build tools, local database/runtime outputs, Codex worktree isolation.
# MainFuncs: Ignore dependency folders, env files, databases, build outputs, backups, exports, `.worktrees/`, and `.claude/`.
# SideEffects: Keeps local-only files untracked.

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.npm-cache/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ...except the frontend's, which CI installs from.
#
# With the lockfile ignored, `npm install` on a CI runner re-resolves every dependency from scratch
# on every run, so no two runs are guaranteed to use the same versions and a green run proves
# nothing about the next one. That is how c40a7f8 failed CI at `npm run build` and `npm test` while
# the same commit passed lint, build AND test on Linux + Node 20.20.2 (the runner's own version)
# with a fresh install, and passed on Windows twice.
#
# The committed lockfile was generated on Linux/Node 20 from that verified tree; it is v3, so it
# records the win32/darwin/linux platform packages too and stays usable on every dev machine.
# Regenerate it deliberately (`npm install`, commit the diff) — never let it drift silently.
!frontend/package-lock.json

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.development
.env.*
*.env

# Database
backend/data/*.db
backend/data/*.db-journal
backend/data/*.db-shm
backend/data/*.db-wal
*.sql
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Logs
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Build outputs
dist/
build/
frontend/dist/
frontend/build/

# Playwright e2e output (regenerated by `npm run test:e2e`)
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# MediaMTX (binaries are downloaded by deployment/download-mediamtx-linux.sh — keep only config)
mediamtx/recordings/
mediamtx/logs/
mediamtx/mediamtx
mediamtx/mediamtx.exe

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
.worktrees/
private_exports/
private_imports/

# Local CCTV import/export and debug artifacts
/tmp_*
/*.dec.txt
/*.sec
/*.apk
/*_import_*.json
/*_raw_*.json
/*_catalog_*.json
/cctv_backup_*.json
/private_exports/

# Claude Code local artifacts (SECURITY)
# settings.local.json is machine-specific, and .claude/tmp/ holds throwaway ops scripts that
# carry live credentials (payment-gateway keys, SSH passwords) — they must never be committed.
#
# Deny-by-default, then re-include ONLY what is meant to be shared. The pattern has to be
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/` — git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# bare `.claude/` makes any `!.claude/<x>` below it silently do nothing.
# Anything not explicitly re-included here stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Backup files (SECURITY)
*.bak
*.backup
*.old
*.orig
*.save

# Config backups (SECURITY)
config.php.bak
config.js.bak
config.json.bak
*.config.bak

# Git directory (SECURITY)
.git/

# Apache configs (SECURITY)
.htaccess
.htpasswd

# SSH keys (SECURITY)
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_rsa.pub

# Certificates (SECURITY)
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx

# Generated client configuration (per-installation)
deployment/client.config.sh

# Python bytecode (sidecar)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
